# Kids sites — deploy after owner OK

When **kids static sites** change (paths rsynced by `top/scripts/deploy-kids-sites.sh`), **do not deploy automatically**.

Follow **`warn-before-live-user-impact`**: give a **Deploy check** (will it mess with readers?) before running the script.

**Deploy only when** the owner clearly says **deploy**, **deploy now**, **ship it**, or **yes** — but **always** the Deploy check **first in the same turn**, then run deploy.

From **repo root** when approved:

```bash
bash top/scripts/deploy-kids-sites.sh
```

**Usually touched paths:** `maestrosOdyssey/www/`, `crocheter/www/`, `envDyst/www/`, `halalit/www/`, `top/directory/www/` (hub), `top/_shared/serve_static_https.py`.

**Halalit:** Same rule for `halalit/www/`. `halalit/.cursor/private/` design-notes are local-only and never deployed.

If SSH or the script fails, say so clearly and leave the command for a retry.

For edits that **do not** affect those deploy paths, skip deploy.
